From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:02:19 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: apple: report a PCIe-C tunnel without preinit at
 info level

On M1 and M2 Macs m1n1 does not bring up the PCIe-C tunnel controller,
and the kernel only cold-initialises it on the generations the PCI
driver admits. Every USB4 port then logged a warning at probe, two on
the M2 and three on the M1 Pro, although the router works and nothing
failed: PCIe tunnelling is not offered on these ports.

Say so once per port at info level. Errors while mapping or resetting a
tunnel that is available are still reported as before.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit f1de4c0d47bdc1c243901a92c73b8d6995d22c11)
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c
index 8f38748504..077d04621c 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c
@@ -3279,7 +3279,7 @@ static int apple_cio_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			apple_cio_pcie_tunnel_is_preinitialized(
 				acio->pcie_tunnel_np);
 		if (!acio->pcie_tunnel_preinitialized) {
-			dev_warn(dev,
+			dev_info(dev,
 				 "PCIe-C tunnel disabled: not initialized by m1n1 or the kernel\n");
 		} else {
 			ret = apple_cio_map_pcie_intr2axi(acio);
